IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-groups`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2, ss 145 to 147: who may be a director, the resident director,
-- resignation, nominee directors, what must be filed before a person is named as a director, and the share qualification.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own
-- words; NOTHING is "the text does not say". A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every JUST FALSE and NOTHING below
-- carries the quoted words or the reason, and NOTES.md (sgb1) lists the fork lines.
-- A bar is named as a bar: JUST TRUE means "the section bars it".
-- Amounts are copied from the text. A fine "not exceeding" is a highest fine. 2 years is written 2 TIMES 12 months.

§ `Section 145: directors`

-- The penalty an offence of this module carries. One record, shared by the offence functions of this module
-- (fields not used by an offence are 0 or FALSE).
DECLARE `s 145(8) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the highest further fine for each day or part of a day during which a continuing offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) first limb: the company must have a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore.
-- src:11596 | 145.—(1) Every company must have at least one director who is
-- src:11597 | ordinarily resident in Singapore and, where the company only has
-- src:11598 | one member, that sole director may also be the sole member of the
-- src:11599 | company.
@ref s 145(1) (src:11596-11599)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company who are ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(1) the company has a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the number of directors of the company who are ordinarily resident in Singapore` AT LEAST 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must have at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore" (a duty not met, the provision's own question)

-- (1) second limb: where the company only has one member, that sole director may also be the sole member.
@ref s 145(1) (src:11597-11599)
GIVEN `the company only has one member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(1) the sole director may also be the sole member of the company` MEANS
    IF `the company only has one member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (a company's or person's liberty, no bar to relieve; S1b ruling 2026S1bC): "where the company only has one member, that sole director may also be the sole member" -- a "where" gate on a liberty that fails; split site (ii), fork SII-01 in NOTES.md (the other reading is JUST FALSE, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- (2) the bar: no person other than a natural person who has attained 18 years and is of full legal capacity may be a director.
-- src:11601 | (2) No person other than a natural person who has attained the age
-- src:11602 | of 18 years and who is otherwise of full legal capacity may be a
-- src:11603 | director of a company.
@ref s 145(2) (src:11601-11603)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the person, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is otherwise of full legal capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(2) the subsection bars the person from being a director of a company` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a natural person`
      AND `the age of the person, in years` AT LEAST 18
      AND `the person is otherwise of full legal capacity`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No person other than a natural person who has attained the age of 18 years and who is otherwise of full legal capacity may be a director" bars the others and says nothing of a person inside the class (other bars, such as ss 148 to 155E, may apply)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3) deleted.
-- (4) a constitution provision in force immediately before 29 December 1967 that made a corporation a director is read as
-- authorising that corporation to appoint a natural person (transitional: inert in NOTES.md, reason 2; the rule is still encoded).
-- src:11609 | (4) Any provision in the constitution of a company which was in
-- src:11610 | force immediately before 29 December 1967 and which operated to
-- src:11611 | constitute a corporation as a director of the company is to be read and
-- src:11616 | construed as if it authorised that corporation to appoint a natural
-- src:11617 | person to be a director of that company.
@ref s 145(4) (src:11609-11617)
GIVEN `the provision of the constitution was in force immediately before 29 December 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision operated to constitute a corporation as a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(4) the provision is read as authorising the corporation to appoint a natural person to be a director` MEANS
    IF `the provision of the constitution was in force immediately before 29 December 1967` AND `the provision operated to constitute a corporation as a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision in the constitution of a company which was in force immediately before 29 December 1967 and which operated to constitute a corporation as a director" -- a scope limit with no "only"

-- (5) and (6): the bar on resigning, and where it does not apply.
-- (6)(b): the grounds on which a director may be required to resign or vacate office, one constructor per instrument the text names.
DECLARE `s 145(6)(b) ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office` IS ONE OF
    `s 145(6)(b) section 148, 149, 149A, 154, 155, 155A or 155C of this Act`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 50 or 54 of the Banking Act 1970`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 50 or 54 of the Banking Act 1970 as applied by section 55ZJ of that Act`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 46(7) of the Credit Bureau Act 2016`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 47 of the Finance Companies Act 1967`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 64 of the Financial Advisers Act 2001`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 62 or 63 of the Financial Holdings Companies Act 2013`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 48 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 35, 36, 88 or 102(2)(a)(ii) of the Insurance Act 1966`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 40 of the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970 as in force immediately before the date of commencement of section 205 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 35 or 66 of the Payment Services Act 2019`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 43, 46Z, 81P, 81ZJ, 97, 123Y, 123ZU or 292A of the Securities and Futures Act 2001`
    `s 145(6)(b) section 14 of the Trust Companies Act 2005`
    `s 145(6)(b) none of these`

-- src:11641 | (6) Subsection (5) does not apply where a director of a company is
-- src:11642 | required to resign or vacate his or her office —
-- src:11644 | (a) if the director has not within the period referred to in
-- src:11645 | section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification; or
-- src:11649 | (b) by virtue of his or her disqualification or removal or the
-- src:11650 | revocation of his or her appointment as a director (as the
-- src:11651 | case may be) under section 148, 149, 149A, 154, 155,
-- src:11652 | 155A or 155C of this Act, section 50 or 54 of the Banking
-- src:11653 | Act 1970, section 50 or 54 of the Banking Act 1970 as
-- src:11654 | applied by section 55ZJ of that Act, section 46(7) of the
-- src:11655 | Credit Bureau Act 2016, section 47 of the Finance
-- src:11656 | Companies Act 1967, section 64 of the Financial
-- src:11657 | Advisers Act 2001, section 62 or 63 of the Financial
-- src:11658 | Holdings Companies Act 2013, section 48 of the Financial
-- src:11659 | Services and Markets Act 2022, section 35, 36, 88 or
-- src:11660 | 102(2)(a)(ii) of the Insurance Act 1966, section 40 of the
-- src:11661 | Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970 as in force
-- src:11662 | immediately before the date of commencement of
-- src:11663 | section 205 of the Financial Services and Markets Act
-- src:11668 | 2022, section 35 or 66 of the Payment Services Act 2019,
-- src:11669 | section 43, 46Z, 81P, 81ZJ, 97, 123Y, 123ZU or 292A of
-- src:11670 | the Securities and Futures Act 2001 and section 14 of the
-- src:11671 | Trust Companies Act 2005.
-- src:11677 | (c) [Deleted by Act 24 of 2025 wef 06/05/2026]
@ref s 145(6) (src:11641-11677)
GIVEN `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` IS A `s 145(6)(b) ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(6) subsection (5) does not apply to the director's resignation or vacation of office` MEANS
    IF `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` EQUALS `s 145(6)(b) none of these`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (5) does not apply where a director of a company is required to resign or vacate his or her office -- (a) if ...; (b) by virtue of his or her disqualification or removal or the revocation of his or her appointment" -- a "where" gate that fails (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:11632 | (5) Despite anything in this Act or in the constitution of the
-- src:11633 | company, or in any agreement with the company, a director of a
-- src:11634 | company must not resign or vacate his or her office unless there is
-- src:11635 | remaining in the company at least one director who is ordinarily
-- src:11636 | resident in Singapore; and any purported resignation or vacation of
-- src:11637 | office in breach of this subsection is invalid.
@ref s 145(5) (src:11632-11637)
GIVEN `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` IS A `s 145(6)(b) ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(5) the subsection bars the director from resigning or vacating office` MEANS
    IF `s 145(6) subsection (5) does not apply to the director's resignation or vacation of office` `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (5) does not apply where a director of a company is required to resign or vacate his or her office" (subsection (6))
    ELSE (IF `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not resign or vacate his or her office unless there is remaining in the company at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore" -- the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 145(5) (src:11634-11637)
GIVEN `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` IS A `s 145(6)(b) ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(5) the purported resignation or vacation of office is invalid` MEANS
    IF `s 145(5) the subsection bars the director from resigning or vacating office` `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any purported resignation or vacation of office in breach of this subsection is invalid" says nothing of one that is not in breach

-- (4A) a director may resign by written notice, unless the constitution otherwise provides, subject to (5).
-- src:11621 | (4A) Subject to subsection (5), unless the constitution otherwise
-- src:11622 | provides, a director of a company may resign by giving the company
-- src:11623 | a written notice of his or her resignation.
@ref s 145(4A) (src:11621-11623)
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director gives the company a written notice of his or her resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` IS A `s 145(6)(b) ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(4A) the director may resign by giving the company a written notice of resignation` MEANS
    IF `the constitution otherwise provides`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the constitution otherwise provides" hands the question to the constitution, which is not among the sources; a grant ("may resign") whose "unless" gate is met by the constitution (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)
    ELSE (IF `s 145(5) the subsection bars the director from resigning or vacating office` `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (5)" and subsection (5): "must not resign or vacate his or her office unless there is remaining in the company at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore"
          ELSE (IF `the director gives the company a written notice of his or her resignation`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may resign by giving the company a written notice" names one way and does not say no to another

-- (4B) the resignation is not conditional upon the company's acceptance, subject to (5).
-- src:11627 | (4B) Subject to subsection (5), the resignation of a director is not
-- src:11628 | conditional upon the company’s acceptance of his or her resignation.
@ref s 145(4B) (src:11627-11628)
GIVEN `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` IS A `s 145(6)(b) ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(4B) the resignation is conditional upon the company's acceptance of it` MEANS
    IF `s 145(5) the subsection bars the director from resigning or vacating office` `at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore would remain in the company` `the director is required to resign or vacate office because the director has not within the period referred to in section 147(1) obtained his or her qualification` `the ground on which the director is required to resign or vacate office by virtue of disqualification, removal or revocation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (5)": where subsection (5) bars the resignation it is invalid, and subsection (4B) says nothing of acceptance
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the resignation of a director is not conditional upon the company's acceptance of his or her resignation"

-- (7) The Registrar may direct the members of the company to appoint a resident director.
-- src:11681 | (7) If there is a contravention of subsection (1), the Registrar may,
-- src:11682 | either of the Registrar’s own motion or on the application of any
-- src:11683 | person, direct the members of the company to appoint a director who
-- src:11684 | is ordinarily resident in Singapore if the Registrar considers it to be in
-- src:11685 | the interests of the company for such appointment to be made.
@ref s 145(7) (src:11681-11685)
GIVEN `there is a contravention of section 145(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar considers it to be in the interests of the company for such appointment to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(7) the Registrar may direct the members of the company to appoint a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `there is a contravention of section 145(1)` AND `the Registrar considers it to be in the interests of the company for such appointment to be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If there is a contravention of subsection (1), the Registrar may ... if the Registrar considers it to be in the interests of the company" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (8) the offence of a member in default of the direction.
-- src:11687 | (8) If the direction under subsection (7) is not complied with, each
-- src:11688 | member in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:11689 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and, in the case of a
-- src:11690 | continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every
-- src:11691 | day or part thereof during which the offence continues after
-- src:11692 | conviction.
@ref s 145(8) (src:11687-11692)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given a direction under section 145(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(8) the member is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has given a direction under section 145(7)` AND `the direction has not been complied with` AND `the person is a member of the company in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If the direction under subsection (7) is not complied with, each member in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 145(8) (src:11687-11692)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given a direction under section 145(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 145(8) penalty`
`s 145(8) the most the member may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 145(8) the member is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the Registrar has given a direction under section 145(7)` `the direction has not been complied with` `the person is a member of the company in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 145(8) penalty` OF 2000, 0, 1000, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $2,000 and, for a continuing offence, a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day after conviction
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the member it makes guilty

-- (9) The Court may order the members to make the appointment.
-- src:11694 | (9) If there is a contravention of subsection (1) and —
-- src:11696 | (a) the Registrar fails to give the direction under
-- src:11697 | subsection (7); or
-- src:11699 | (b) such direction has been given but is not complied with,
-- src:11701 | the Court may, on the application of the Registrar or any person, order
-- src:11702 | the members of the company to make the appointment if it considers
-- src:11703 | it to be in the interests of the company for such appointment to be
-- src:11704 | made.
@ref s 145(9) (src:11694-11704)
GIVEN `there is a contravention of section 145(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar fails to give the direction under section 145(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction under section 145(7) has been given but is not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Registrar or by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court considers it to be in the interests of the company for such appointment to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(9) the Court may order the members of the company to make the appointment` MEANS
    IF    `there is a contravention of section 145(1)`
      AND (`the Registrar fails to give the direction under section 145(7)` OR `the direction under section 145(7) has been given but is not complied with`)
      AND `the application is made by the Registrar or by any person`
      AND `the Court considers it to be in the interests of the company for such appointment to be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If there is a contravention of subsection (1) and (a) ... or (b) ..., the Court may, on the application of the Registrar or any person, order ... if it considers it to be in the interests of the company" -- a grant ("may") whose "if" gate failed (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md)

-- (10) a member who knows is liable for the debts contracted after the company has carried on business for more than 6 months
-- without a resident director.
-- src:11708 | (10) If a company carries on business without having at least
-- src:11709 | one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore for more than
-- src:11710 | 6 months, a person who, for the whole or any part of the period that it
-- src:11711 | so carries on business after those 6 months —
-- src:11713 | (a) is a member of the company; and
-- src:11715 | (b) knows that it is carrying on business in that manner,
-- src:11720 | shall be liable for the payment of all the debts of the company
-- src:11721 | contracted during the period or that part of the period (as the case may
-- src:11722 | be), and may be sued therefor.
@ref s 145(10) (src:11708-11722)
GIVEN `the number of months for which the company has carried on business without a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is a member of the company for the whole or any part of the period after those 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the company is carrying on business in that manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(10) the member is liable for the payment of the debts of the company` MEANS
    IF    `the number of months for which the company has carried on business without a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore` GREATER THAN 6
      AND `the person is a member of the company for the whole or any part of the period after those 6 months`
      AND `the person knows that the company is carrying on business in that manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If a company carries on business without having at least one director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore for more than 6 months, a person who ... (a) is a member of the company; and (b) knows that it is carrying on business in that manner, shall be liable" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 145(10) (src:11720-11722)
GIVEN `the number of months for which the company has carried on business without a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is a member of the company for the whole or any part of the period after those 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the company is carrying on business in that manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt was contracted during the period or that part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(10) the debt is within the liability of the member` MEANS
    IF `s 145(10) the member is liable for the payment of the debts of the company` `the number of months for which the company has carried on business without a director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore` `the person is a member of the company for the whole or any part of the period after those 6 months` `the person knows that the company is carrying on business in that manner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `the debt was contracted during the period or that part of the period`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable for the payment of all the debts of the company contracted during the period or that part of the period" says nothing of a debt contracted outside it
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i)): the member is not liable under this subsection

§ `Regulative rules: section 145(5), the bar on resigning`

DECLARE `s 145(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 145(5) resign or vacate office leaving no director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore`

-- (5): the prohibition derived from the flat negative "must not resign or vacate his or her office unless" (N2 of 2026-11-04: the bearer is named, the director).
-- No time limit: no trace shows a late act; the forbidden act is the breach.
-- src:11632 | (5) Despite anything in this Act or in the constitution of the
-- src:11633 | company, or in any agreement with the company, a director of a
-- src:11634 | company must not resign or vacate his or her office unless there is
-- src:11635 | remaining in the company at least one director who is ordinarily
-- src:11636 | resident in Singapore; and any purported resignation or vacation of
-- src:11637 | office in breach of this subsection is invalid.
@ref s 145(5) (src:11632-11637)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 145(5) act`
`s 145(5) a director must not resign or vacate office leaving no director ordinarily resident in Singapore` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    SHANT `s 145(5) resign or vacate office leaving no director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director resigned or vacated office with no director who is ordinarily resident in Singapore remaining in the company"

§ `Section 145A: acting as a nominee director`

DECLARE `s 145A(3) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the highest further fine for each day or part of a day during which a continuing offence continues after conviction, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- (4) "nominee director" means a director who is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in
-- accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person.
-- src:11763 | “nominee director” means a director who is accustomed or
-- src:11764 | under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in
-- src:11769 | accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any
-- src:11770 | other person.
@ref s 145A(4) "nominee director" (src:11763-11770)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is accustomed to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(4) "nominee director" the person is a nominee director` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director of the company`
      AND (`the director is accustomed to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person` OR `the director is under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“nominee director” means a director who is accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person" (a "means" definition)

-- (4) "affiliated company", in relation to a person: (a) a company that employs the person; (b) a company which by virtue of s 6
-- is deemed to be related to a corporation that employs the person. Limb (b) takes the s 6 answer from the keel.
-- src:11751 | (4) In this section —
-- src:11753 | “affiliated company”, in relation to a person, means —
-- src:11755 | (a) a company that employs the person; or
-- src:11757 | (b) a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to
-- src:11758 | be related to a corporation that employs the person;
@ref s 145A(4) "affiliated company" (src:11751-11758)
GIVEN `the company employs the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is deemed to be related by virtue of section 6 to a corporation that employs the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(4) "affiliated company" the company is an affiliated company of the person` MEANS
    IF    `the company employs the person`
       OR (`s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` `the company is deemed to be related by virtue of section 6 to a corporation that employs the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“affiliated company”, in relation to a person, means -- (a) a company that employs the person; or (b) a company which by virtue of section 6 is deemed to be related to a corporation that employs the person" (a "means" definition)

-- (4) "appointed day" means the date of commencement of section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024: a supplied date.
-- src:11760 | “appointed day” means the date of commencement of
-- src:11761 | section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024;
@ref s 145A(4) "appointed day" (src:11760-11761)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date of commencement of section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(4) "appointed day" the date asked is on or after the appointed day` MEANS
    IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date of commencement of section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“appointed day” means the date of commencement of section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024" (a "means" definition: a date before it is not on or after the appointed day)

-- (1) and (2): a person must not act as a nominee director by way of business on or after the appointed day, unless
-- (a) a registered corporate service provider for the service, or (b) the acting is arranged by one; (2) not where the person acts
-- for an affiliated company or began before the appointed day.
-- src:11726 | 145A.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person must not, on or after
-- src:11727 | the appointed day, act as a nominee director of a company by way of
-- src:11728 | business, unless —
-- src:11730 | (a) the person is a registered corporate service provider for
-- src:11731 | providing the corporate service of acting, or arranging for
-- src:11732 | another person to act as a director of a corporation; or
-- src:11734 | (b) his or her so acting is arranged by a registered corporate
-- src:11735 | service provider for that corporate service.
-- src:11737 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply where —
-- src:11739 | (a) the person acts as a nominee director of his or her affiliated
-- src:11740 | company; or
-- src:11742 | (b) the person had commenced acting as a nominee director of
-- src:11743 | the company before the appointed day.
@ref s 145A(1) (src:11726-11743)
GIVEN `the person acts as a nominee director of the company by way of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person acts` IS A DATE
      `the date of commencement of section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024` IS A DATE
      `the person is a registered corporate service provider as section 2(1) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024 gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registration covers the corporate service of acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a director of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's acting is arranged by a registered corporate service provider for that corporate service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is an affiliated company of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had commenced acting as a nominee director of the company before the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(1) the subsection bars the person from acting as a nominee director of the company by way of business` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person acts as a nominee director of the company by way of business`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person must not ... act as a nominee director of a company by way of business" -- a scope limit with no "only"
    ELSE (IF `s 145A(4) "appointed day" the date asked is on or after the appointed day` `the date the person acts` `the date of commencement of section 38(b) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024` EQUALS JUST FALSE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on or after the appointed day" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
          ELSE (IF    (`s 4(1) "registered corporate service provider" the person is a registered corporate service provider` `the person is a registered corporate service provider as section 2(1) of the Corporate Service Providers Act 2024 gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the registration covers the corporate service of acting, or arranging for another person to act, as a director of a corporation`)
                   OR `the person's acting is arranged by a registered corporate service provider for that corporate service`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not ... unless -- (a) the person is a registered corporate service provider ...; or (b) his or her so acting is arranged by a registered corporate service provider" -- the "unless" is met
                ELSE (IF `the company is an affiliated company of the person` OR `the person had commenced acting as a nominee director of the company before the appointed day`
                      THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply where -- (a) the person acts as a nominee director of his or her affiliated company; or (b) the person had commenced acting as a nominee director of the company before the appointed day"
                      ELSE JUST TRUE)))

-- src:11745 | (3) Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an
-- src:11746 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:11747 | $10,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:11748 | exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:11749 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 145A(3) (src:11745-11749)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 145A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 145A(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Any person who contravenes subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence" -- the element is unmet

@ref s 145A(3) (src:11745-11749)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 145A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 145A(3) penalty`
`s 145A(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 145A(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person contravenes section 145A(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 145A(3) penalty` OF 10000, 1000)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 and, for a continuing offence, a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day after conviction
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

DECLARE `s 145A(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 145A(1) act as a nominee director of a company by way of business on or after the appointed day, neither as nor through a registered corporate service provider`

-- (1): the prohibition. The act is the forbidden conduct; there is no time limit, so the breach is the act.
-- src:11726 | 145A.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), a person must not, on or after
-- src:11727 | the appointed day, act as a nominee director of a company by way of
-- src:11728 | business, unless —
-- src:11730 | (a) the person is a registered corporate service provider for
-- src:11731 | providing the corporate service of acting, or arranging for
-- src:11732 | another person to act as a director of a corporation; or
-- src:11734 | (b) his or her so acting is arranged by a registered corporate
-- src:11735 | service provider for that corporate service.
@ref s 145A(1) (src:11726-11735)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 145A(1) act`
`s 145A(1) a person must not act as a nominee director by way of business unless a registered corporate service provider` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 145A(1) act as a nominee director of a company by way of business on or after the appointed day, neither as nor through a registered corporate service provider`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person acted as a nominee director of a company by way of business without being, or being arranged by, a registered corporate service provider"

§ `Section 146: who may be named as a director, and what must be filed first`

DECLARE `s 146(4) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1A)(a): the three filings with the Registrar, by the person or through a registered qualified individual.
-- src:11799 | (1A) The conditions to be complied with by a person referred to in
-- src:11800 | subsection (1) are the following:
-- src:11802 | (a) the person has, by himself or herself or through a registered
-- src:11803 | qualified individual authorised by him or her, filed with the
-- src:11804 | Registrar —
-- src:11806 | (i) a declaration that he or she has consented to act as a
-- src:11807 | director;
-- src:11809 | (ii) a statement in the prescribed form that he or she is
-- src:11810 | not disqualified from acting as a director under this
-- src:11811 | Act; and
-- src:11813 | (iii) a statement in the prescribed form that he or she is
-- src:11814 | not debarred under section 155B from acting as
-- src:11815 | director of the company;
@ref s 146(1A)(a) (src:11799-11815)
GIVEN `the person has filed a declaration that the person has consented to act as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has filed a statement in the prescribed form that the person is not disqualified from acting as a director under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has filed a statement in the prescribed form that the person is not debarred under section 155B from acting as director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(1A)(a) the person has made the filings paragraph (a) requires` MEANS
    IF    `the person has filed a declaration that the person has consented to act as a director`
      AND `the person has filed a statement in the prescribed form that the person is not disqualified from acting as a director under this Act`
      AND `the person has filed a statement in the prescribed form that the person is not debarred under section 155B from acting as director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions to be complied with by a person referred to in subsection (1) are the following: (a) the person has ... filed with the Registrar -- (i) ...; (ii) ...; and (iii) ..." (a condition not met, the provision's own question)

-- (1A)(b): one of four filings about the share qualification.
-- src:11820 | (b) the person has, by himself or herself or through a registered
-- src:11821 | qualified individual authorised by him or her —
-- src:11823 | (i) filed with the Registrar a declaration that the person
-- src:11824 | has agreed to take a number of shares of the company
-- src:11825 | that is not less than the person’s qualification, if any;
-- src:11827 | (ii) filed with the Registrar an undertaking that the
-- src:11828 | person will take from the company and pay for his or
-- src:11829 | her qualification shares, if any;
-- src:11831 | (iii) filed with the Registrar a declaration that a specified
-- src:11832 | number of shares, not less than the person’s
-- src:11833 | qualification (if any), has been registered in the
-- src:11834 | person’s name; or
-- src:11836 | (iv) in the case of a company formed or intended to be
-- src:11837 | formed by way of reconstruction of another
-- src:11838 | corporation or group of corporations or to acquire
-- src:11839 | the shares in another corporation or group of
-- src:11840 | corporations, filed with the Registrar a declaration
-- src:11841 | that —
-- src:11843 | (A) the person was a shareholder in that other
-- src:11844 | corporation or in one or more of the
-- src:11845 | corporations of that group; and
-- src:11847 | (B) as a shareholder the person will be entitled to
-- src:11848 | receive and have registered in his or her name a
-- src:11849 | number of shares not less than his or her
-- src:11850 | qualification, by virtue of the terms of an
-- src:11851 | agreement relating to the reconstruction.
@ref s 146(1A)(b) (src:11820-11851)
GIVEN `the person has filed a declaration that the person has agreed to take a number of shares of the company that is not less than the person's qualification, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has filed an undertaking that the person will take from the company and pay for his or her qualification shares, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has filed a declaration that a specified number of shares, not less than the person's qualification (if any), has been registered in the person's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is formed or intended to be formed by way of reconstruction of another corporation or group of corporations or to acquire the shares in another corporation or group of corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has filed a declaration that the person was a shareholder in that other corporation or group and will be entitled to receive and have registered in his or her name a number of shares not less than his or her qualification, by virtue of the terms of an agreement relating to the reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(1A)(b) the person has made the filing paragraph (b) requires` MEANS
    IF    `the person has filed a declaration that the person has agreed to take a number of shares of the company that is not less than the person's qualification, if any`
       OR `the person has filed an undertaking that the person will take from the company and pay for his or her qualification shares, if any`
       OR `the person has filed a declaration that a specified number of shares, not less than the person's qualification (if any), has been registered in the person's name`
       OR (`the company is formed or intended to be formed by way of reconstruction of another corporation or group of corporations or to acquire the shares in another corporation or group of corporations` AND `the person has filed a declaration that the person was a shareholder in that other corporation or group and will be entitled to receive and have registered in his or her name a number of shares not less than his or her qualification, by virtue of the terms of an agreement relating to the reconstruction`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the person has ... (i) filed ...; (ii) filed ...; (iii) filed ...; or (iv) in the case of a company formed ... by way of reconstruction ..., filed" -- none of the four filings (a condition not met, the provision's own question)

-- (3)(c): the one-year limit measured from the day the company was entitled to commence business.
-- src:11872 | (c) a prospectus or a statement in lieu of prospectus issued or
-- src:11873 | lodged with the Registrar by or on behalf of a company or
-- src:11874 | to a constitution adopted by a company after the expiration
-- src:11875 | of one year from the date on which the company was
-- src:11876 | entitled to commence business.
@ref s 146(3)(c) (src:11872-11876)
GIVEN `the document is a prospectus or a statement in lieu of prospectus issued or lodged with the Registrar by or on behalf of the company, or a constitution adopted by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the document was issued, lodged or adopted` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company was entitled to commence business` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(3)(c) the document is outside subsections (1) and (2) by reason of paragraph (c)` MEANS
    IF `the document is a prospectus or a statement in lieu of prospectus issued or lodged with the Registrar by or on behalf of the company, or a constitution adopted by the company`
    THEN (IF `the date the document was issued, lodged or adopted` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date on which the company was entitled to commence business` 1 Years
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the expiration of one year from the date on which the company was entitled to commence business" -- a document within the year is not said to be inside or outside
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) names a prospectus, a statement in lieu of prospectus or a constitution

-- (3): (1) and (2), other than the provisions relating to signing a consent to act as director, do not apply to
-- (a) a company not having a share capital; (b) a private company; (c) as above.
-- READING (fork F-146-1, marginal, for a lawyer): of the conditions of (1A), only the consent to act (1A)(a)(i) is a provision "relating to
-- the signing of a consent to act as director"; the other filings are outside (1) for these companies.
-- src:11862 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) (other than the provisions relating to the
-- src:11863 | signing of a consent to act as director) do not apply to —
-- src:11865 | (a) a company not having a share capital;
-- src:11870 | (b) a private company; or
-- src:11872 | (c) a prospectus or a statement in lieu of prospectus issued or
-- src:11873 | lodged with the Registrar by or on behalf of a company or
-- src:11874 | to a constitution adopted by a company after the expiration
-- src:11875 | of one year from the date on which the company was
-- src:11876 | entitled to commence business.
@ref s 146(3) (src:11862-11876)
GIVEN `the company has no share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c) of section 146(3) applies to the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(3) the requirements of subsections (1) and (2), other than the provisions relating to the signing of a consent to act as director, do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the company has no share capital` OR `the company is a private company` OR `paragraph (c) of section 146(3) applies to the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) (other than the provisions relating to the signing of a consent to act as director) do not apply to -- (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." -- none of the three heads holds, so the exemption the subsection gives does not apply (hand-off ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a), for a list the text hands the exemption to)

-- (1): the bar on being named in a document filed for incorporation or in the register, unless the (1A) conditions were met first.
DECLARE `s 146(1) where the person is named as a director or proposed director` IS ONE OF
    `s 146(1)(a) in a document filed or lodged with or submitted to the Registrar for the purposes of the incorporation of a company`
    `s 146(1)(b) in the register of directors, chief executive officers and secretaries of a company`
    `s 146(1) somewhere else`

-- src:11776 | 146.—(1) A person must not be named as a director or proposed
-- src:11777 | director in —
-- src:11779 | (a) any document filed or lodged with or submitted to the
-- src:11780 | Registrar for the purposes of the incorporation of a
-- src:11781 | company; or
-- src:11783 | (b) the register of directors, chief executive officers and
-- src:11784 | secretaries of a company,
-- src:11786 | unless, before —
-- src:11788 | (c) the incorporation of the company; or
-- src:11790 | (d) the filing of any return in the prescribed form containing
-- src:11791 | the particulars required to be specified in the register of
-- src:11792 | directors, chief executive officers and secretaries,
-- src:11794 | as the case may be, the person has complied with the conditions set
-- src:11795 | out in subsection (1A).
@ref s 146(1) (src:11776-11795)
GIVEN `where the person is named` IS A `s 146(1) where the person is named as a director or proposed director`
      `the person made the filings paragraph (a) of subsection (1A) requires before the incorporation or the filing of the return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made the filing paragraph (b) of subsection (1A) requires before the incorporation or the filing of the return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of subsections (1) and (2), other than the provisions relating to the signing of a consent to act as director, do not apply to the company or the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has filed a declaration that the person has consented to act as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(1) the subsection bars the person from being named as a director or proposed director` MEANS
    IF `where the person is named` EQUALS `s 146(1) somewhere else`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person must not be named as a director or proposed director in (a) any document filed ... for the purposes of the incorporation of a company; or (b) the register of directors, chief executive officers and secretaries" -- other places are not named
    ELSE (IF `the requirements of subsections (1) and (2), other than the provisions relating to the signing of a consent to act as director, do not apply to the company or the document`
          THEN (IF `the person has filed a declaration that the person has consented to act as a director`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, before ... the person has complied with the conditions set out in subsection (1A)" -- the consent, the only condition that survives subsection (3), was filed
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the person made the filings paragraph (a) of subsection (1A) requires before the incorporation or the filing of the return` AND `the person made the filing paragraph (b) of subsection (1A) requires before the incorporation or the filing of the return`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person must not be named ... unless, before ... the person has complied with the conditions set out in subsection (1A)" -- the "unless" is met
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- (2): a person who undertook under (1A)(b)(ii) is in the same position as a subscriber for those shares.
-- src:11855 | (2) Where a person has undertaken to the Registrar under
-- src:11856 | subsection (1A)(b)(ii) to take and pay for the person’s qualification
-- src:11857 | shares, the person is, as regards those shares, in the same position as if
-- src:11858 | the person had signed the constitution for that number of shares.
@ref s 146(2) (src:11855-11858)
GIVEN `the person has undertaken to the Registrar under subsection (1A)(b)(ii) to take and pay for the person's qualification shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(2) the person is, as regards those shares, in the same position as if the person had signed the constitution for that number of shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has undertaken to the Registrar under subsection (1A)(b)(ii) to take and pay for the person's qualification shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person has undertaken to the Registrar under subsection (1A)(b)(ii) ..., the person is, as regards those shares, in the same position" -- a "where" gate that fails (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- (4): the offence of default, by the company and every officer in default; fine and a default penalty.
-- src:11880 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:11881 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:11882 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:11883 | $10,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 146(4) (src:11880-11883)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 146` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 146` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 146(4) (src:11880-11883)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 146` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 146(4) penalty`
`s 146(4) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 146(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 146` `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 146(4) penalty` OF 10000, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 and also a default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (5): the restrictions in relation to a prospectus apply to a director or proposed director of a foreign company.
-- src:11885 | (5) The restrictions in this section on a director or proposed director
-- src:11886 | of a company incorporated under this Act in relation to a prospectus
-- src:11887 | apply in the same manner and extent to a director or proposed director
-- src:11888 | of a foreign company as if the references in subsections (1) and (4) to
-- src:11889 | a company included references to a foreign company.
@ref s 146(5) (src:11885-11889)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is one in relation to a prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 146(5) the restrictions apply to a director or proposed director of the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a foreign company` AND `the restriction is one in relation to a prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The restrictions in this section on a director or proposed director of a company incorporated under this Act in relation to a prospectus apply ... to a director or proposed director of a foreign company" -- a scope limit with no "only"

§ `Section 147: the share qualification`

DECLARE `s 147(4) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): the last day for obtaining the qualification: within 2 months after appointment, or any shorter period the constitution fixes.
-- src:11893 | 147.—(1) Without affecting the operation of sections 145 and 146,
-- src:11894 | every director, who is by the constitution required to hold a specified
-- src:11895 | share qualification and who is not already qualified, must obtain his
-- src:11896 | or her qualification within 2 months after his or her appointment or
-- src:11897 | such shorter period as is fixed by the constitution.
@ref s 147(1) (src:11893-11897)
GIVEN `the date of the director's appointment` IS A DATE
      `the constitution fixes a period shorter than 2 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period the constitution fixes, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 147(1) the last day on which the director must have obtained the qualification` MEANS
    IF `the constitution fixes a period shorter than 2 months`
    THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the director's appointment` `the shorter period the constitution fixes, in days` Days
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the director's appointment` 2 Months

