      `the director is not already qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the director's appointment` IS A DATE
      `the constitution fixes a period shorter than 2 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shorter period the constitution fixes, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the director obtained the qualification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 147(1) the director has obtained the qualification in time` MEANS
    IF `the constitution requires the director to hold a specified share qualification` AND `the director is not already qualified`
    THEN (IF `the date the director obtained the qualification` AT MOST `s 147(1) the last day on which the director must have obtained the qualification` `the date of the director's appointment` `the constitution fixes a period shorter than 2 months` `the shorter period the constitution fixes, in days`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must obtain his or her qualification within 2 months after his or her appointment or such shorter period as is fixed by the constitution" -- a period fixed in its own words, outside it (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every director, who is by the constitution required to hold a specified share qualification and who is not already qualified" -- a scope limit with no "only"

